/*=============================================================================
	ArcTerrainTessellationPredicate.ush — the replaceable tessellation metric.

	CONTRACT, both directions:

	  * The predicate does NOT know the CBT representation. Its whole input is
	    three corners in a face's [0,1]^2 domain, the apex of the triangle whose
	    visibility governs (see below), the face id (which names only the face's
	    global texel ORIGIN — the atlas slice comes from the residency ring), the
	    triangle's LEB depth, and the view block below. No node id, no pool slot, no
	    heap, no neighbour reference reaches this file.
	  * The topology code does NOT know how the error is computed. It calls
	    ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangle once per triangle it wants an opinion on and
	    reads back one code. Replacing the metric means replacing this file and
	    the uniforms it declares — nothing in the split/merge machinery moves.

	Consequences of the first half that are easy to break:

	  * DEPTH IS NEVER A MEASURE OF ERROR.
	  * CORNER ORDER IS NOT AN INPUT. leb_DecodeTransformationMatrix_Square
	    applies a winding matrix that swaps corners 0 and 2 on alternate depths, so
	    anything reading orientation off the cross product would be wrong for half
	    the tree. The area below is the ABSOLUTE value of a determinant, which is the
	    same number under either winding and under any permutation of the corners.

	METRIC: the triangle's own area, in square pixels of the MAIN VIEW, after
	projection through the clip transform — the reference criterion (AnisB/large_cbt,
	HPG 2024). Foreshortening is therefore part of the measurement and needs no
	special case: a vertical face seen edge-on projects to nothing and keeps no
	triangles, the same face seen flat-on projects large and gets them.

	Above the EFFECTIVE area target the triangle is too coarse; below that same target
	times MergeThresholdFraction it is finer than the view needs. The two thresholds are
	never equal: a single threshold oscillates split/merge on a camera sitting on it. The
	effective target is TargetTrianglePixels scaled by the flat-area relief below — one
	number, used by BOTH comparisons, or the hysteresis gap moves with the terrain.

	AGREEMENT INSIDE A DIAMOND. The area of a triangle is NOT shared by the two
	parents of a diamond, and nothing requires it to be: the merge command is written
	on the PARENT's verdict, the two children of one parent classify that same parent
	and so read the same number by construction, and ApplyMerge collapses a diamond
	only when all four members carry MERGE (ArcTerrainCBTSplitMerge.usf,
	ARC_CBT_COUNTER_MERGE_NOT_UNANIM). Two parents that disagree simply do not merge.
	The split side never needed agreement at all — a pair splits when EITHER member
	votes for it. All the topology asks of this file is that the verdict be a PURE
	FUNCTION of (Face, Depth, corners, cull apex); every branch below is.

	CONTENT TERM: the sag a split would REMOVE, measured live off the height atlas —
	the edge's sag against its chord, less whatever the deeper of the two halves would
	still carry. A step in the heightmap survives its own bisection unchanged, so this
	reads zero there and a cliff buys no triangles at any depth. It is a LENGTH,
	projected angularly at its own distance and compared against TargetErrorPixels; it
	sits BESIDE the area term as a split vote of its own, and it ALSO scales the area
	target: FLAT-AREA RELIEF. A triangle whose split would remove no sag at all may cover
	FlatAreaRelief times the target, the relief being withdrawn linearly as the sag PER
	SQUARE METRE OF SPLIT EDGE rises to FlatReliefSagCmPerMeterSq. That quotient, and not
	the sag itself, is what the relief reads: a smooth surface hands a parent and its
	children the same reading and so the same effective target, which is what keeps a
	child that votes TOO_FINE from facing a parent that reads TOO_COARSE and refuses the
	merge.

	RESIDENCY CAP: a triangle whose three corners all sample the fill slice is flat by
	construction, so its depth is capped where a leaf covers one sector. The cap is a
	CEILING, not a target: below it the metric decides untouched, and only there can a
	triangle still read TOO_COARSE. As a target it would force a sector-sized leaf over
	the whole world.

	VISIBILITY IS PART OF THE VERDICT, AGAINST A WIDER FRUSTUM THAN THE DRAW'S. A sampled triangle outside
	the TessFrustumCullMargin first tests the full authored-height prism. A wholly rejected prism reads
	TOO_FINE. A prism that can still enter the view uses a bounded planar discovery score: above its split
	target it refines, inside its split/merge deadband it keeps, and only below its merge threshold does it
	pay the full seven-sample metric. That full metric is a MERGE VETO only in the guarded halo: both policies
	must say TOO_FINE before topology may collapse, while a full-metric TOO_COARSE becomes KEEP rather than
	refining the broad conservative prism. The draw's own margin is tighter, so the band between them remains
	geometry prepared for a camera turn without letting the global height range fill the pool.

	BUT THE TRIANGLE JUDGED IS THE ONE THE MERGE IS ABOUT — the caller names it, as CullApex against this
	triangle's own C0 and C2. Coarsening is a decision about the PARENT, and the frustum test is a step: a
	leaf judged on ITSELF gets culled in a band one diamond thick where its parent still crosses the margin,
	and there the leaf reads TOO_FINE against a parent that measures its true area and reads TOO_COARSE, so
	the merge gate refuses forever. Judged on the parent's three corners the leaf and the parent read the SAME test on the SAME sampled
	points, and the band is empty by construction. A merge candidate is itself judged with the cull footprint
	it will receive as a live leaf after the merge, preventing the next frame from switching to its grandparent
	footprint. A caller with no parent to name (the base mesh's split-only vote, and a depth-1 root, which
	merges into nothing) passes its own apex and is judged on itself.

	NO FAR THRESHOLD. The angular edge criterion this replaces needed one: over a
	ground plane it holds a leaf's screen EDGE constant, which puts C/R triangles in an
	annulus at radius R and diverges as ln(R). Screen AREA falls off as 1/R^3 over the
	same plane once the grazing cosine is counted, which puts C/R^2 triangles there —
	convergent, so distance bounds itself and a second threshold has nothing to fix.
=============================================================================*/

#pragma once

#include "/Engine/Public/Platform.ush"
#include "/Plugin/ArcTerrain/ArcTerrainResidencyRing.ush"

/** Verdicts. Negative = the triangle is worth less than it costs, positive = worth more. */
#define ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE        -1
#define ARC_TESS_KEEP             0
#define ARC_TESS_TOO_COARSE       1

/** Which visibility policy produced the verdict. Kept explicit so diagnostics never infer a guarded
 *  decision from zero-valued metric terms. */
#define ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_ORDINARY       0u
#define ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_PRISM_CULLED   1u
#define ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_PRISM_GUARDED  2u

/** Which height range the authored prism consumed. UNKNOWN is reserved for triangles whose sampled
 *  surface never reached the prism test. */
#define ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_UNKNOWN        0u
#define ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_LOCAL          1u
#define ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_FILL           2u
#define ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_SPAN    3u
#define ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_UNSAFE  4u

// --- Content block -----------------------------------------------------------

Texture2DArray<float> HeightAtlas;
SamplerState HeightSamplerBilinear;

/** GLOBAL TEXEL INDEX of each face's (0,0) corner, indexed by face id. Integer, not centimetres: it is
 *  the only form in which the camera can be subtracted without the terrain's absolute extent eating the
 *  metre-scale edge the metric is measuring. */
Buffer<uint2> FaceTexelOrigins;

/** Sector-keyed atlas slice lookup, all tiers concatenated — see arc_HeightRingIndexForTier. */
Buffer<uint> HeightRing;
Buffer<float2> HeightSliceBounds;
uint4 HeightRingOffset;
int4  HeightRingRadius;
int4  HeightRingCenterX;
int4  HeightRingCenterY;
int4  HeightCumulativeShift;
uint  NumHeightTiers;
uint  HeightFillSlice;
uint  HeightSliceBoundsCount;
uint  LocalHeightBoundsEnabled;
float BaseHeightCm;

/** Camera position in the same global texel lattice, split into an exact integer and its remainder. */
int2   CameraTexel;
float2 CameraTexelFrac;

uint  FaceQuads;           // quads per FACE side — the domain a [0,1]^2 corner scales into
// SIGNED on purpose: HLSL promotes int >> uint to an UNSIGNED shift, which turns the arithmetic shift
// this relies on (floor division across the origin) into garbage for negative sector keys.
int   SectorQuadsShift;    // log2(quads per SECTOR side): SectorKey = GlobalTexel >> this
float InvTileResolution;   // 1 / (SectorQuads + 3)
float TexelToLocalCm;

// --- View block --------------------------------------------------------------
// Planar quantities are EYE-RELATIVE TERRAIN-LOCAL centimetres, reached by subtracting
// the camera's texel index from the corner's IN INTEGERS and scaling the difference —
// so the camera sits at the origin and no float ever holds the terrain's extent.

/** Camera height in terrain-local cm: the one axis the atlas sample cannot deliver pre-subtracted. */
float ViewHeightLocalCm;
/** EYE-RELATIVE terrain-local cm -> clip, composed against the terrain transform on the CPU. The shader
 *  never builds a world position: at planet scale a float32 cm has a metre-wide ULP. */
float4x4 EyeLocalToClip;
float2 ViewportSize;
/** Viewport pixels subtended by one radian at the view centre: ViewportHeight / (2 * tan(HalfFOVY)). */
float PixelsPerRadian;
float TargetTrianglePixels;
float MaxTriangleEdgePixels;
float MergeThresholdFraction;
float TargetErrorPixels;
/** Factor on the AREA target where the measured surface matches its triangle plane: the one way the content term subtracts
 *  triangles instead of only adding them. */
float FlatAreaRelief;
/** Sampled deviation, in cm per square metre of longest-edge span, at which that relief is withdrawn. */
float FlatReliefSagCmPerMeterSq;
/** How far past the frustum's side planes a triangle still counts as visible, as a FRACTION of the view's
 *  half-extent: 0.25 tests against a frustum a quarter wider and taller than the screen. Angular, so the
 *  band it holds is the same share of the screen at every distance. */
float FrustumCullMargin;
/** The same widening, for the VERDICT rather than the draw, and deliberately the larger of the two: the
 *  band between them is held at full density but never drawn. */
float TessFrustumCullMargin;
/** Authored local-height contract, resolved to finite ascending values on the render thread. The height
 *  prism consumes it in the next checkpoint; publishing it here keeps every predicate pass in lockstep. */
float2 ConservativeHeightRangeCm;

/** Clip w at or below which the perspective divide has no meaning: the eye plane, one centimetre forward. */
#define ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W 1.0f

/** The subdivision ceiling the topology enforces for every resident height sample. */
int ResidentCapDepth;

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

/** Depth at which a leaf covers exactly one sector: FaceQuads^2 / 2^Depth == (1 << SectorQuadsShift)^2. */
uint ArcTerrainTess_FillCapDepth()
{
	return (uint)max(2 * ((int)firstbithigh(FaceQuads) - SectorQuadsShift), 0);
}

struct FArcTerrainTessTierHit
{
	uint Slice;
	uint Tier;
};

FArcTerrainTessTierHit ArcTerrainTess_ResolveHeightTier(int2 GlobalTexel)
{
	FArcTerrainTessTierHit Hit;
	Hit.Slice = HeightFillSlice;
	Hit.Tier = NumHeightTiers;

	UNROLL
	for (uint T = 0; T < 4u; ++T)
	{
		if (T >= NumHeightTiers)
		{
			break;
		}

		const int Index = arc_HeightRingIndexForTier(GlobalTexel, SectorQuadsShift, T,
			HeightRingOffset, HeightRingRadius, HeightRingCenterX, HeightRingCenterY,
			HeightCumulativeShift);
		if (Index < 0)
		{
			continue;
		}

		const uint Slice = HeightRing[(uint)Index];
		if (Slice != HeightFillSlice)
		{
			Hit.Slice = Slice;
			Hit.Tier = T;
			break;
		}
	}

	return Hit;
}

/** Tier == NumHeightTiers is the "no tier resolved" answer and carries shift 0 into the fill-slice
 *  sample address without indexing past the components the ladder wrote. */
int ArcTerrainTess_HeightTierShift(uint Tier)
{
	int Shift = 0;
	UNROLL
	for (uint T = 0; T < 4u; ++T)
	{
		if (T < NumHeightTiers && T == Tier)
		{
			Shift = HeightCumulativeShift[T];
		}
	}
	return Shift;
}

uint ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(uint Tier)
{
	return Tier < NumHeightTiers ? Tier : 0u;
}

uint ArcTerrainTess_LeafTier(uint Tier0, uint Tier1, uint Tier2)
{
	return max(max(ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(Tier0), ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(Tier1)),
		ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(Tier2));
}

/** HeightCm is TERRAIN-LOCAL, PlanarCm is EYE-RELATIVE terrain-local — the deviation differences the
 *  first, the area and distance terms the second. */
struct FArcTerrainTessSample
{
	float2 PlanarCm;
	float  HeightCm;
	int2   GlobalTexel;
	int2   SectorKey;
	uint   Slice;
	uint   Tier;
	bool   bResident;
};

/** The precision-sensitive, no-height half of ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint. Keeping the whole texel
 *  and its fraction together lets draw-only tests use the exact same camera-relative planar mapping
 *  without resolving residency or sampling the height atlas. */
struct FArcTerrainTessPlanarPoint
{
	int2 GlobalTexel;
	float2 PointFrac;
	float2 PlanarCm;
};

FArcTerrainTessPlanarPoint ArcTerrainTess_ResolvePlanarPoint(uint Face, float2 FacePoint,
	int2 ReferenceCameraTexel, float2 ReferenceCameraTexelFrac)
{
	const float2 PointTexel = FacePoint * float(FaceQuads);
	const int2 PointWhole = int2(floor(PointTexel));

	FArcTerrainTessPlanarPoint Point;
	Point.PointFrac = PointTexel - float2(PointWhole);
	Point.GlobalTexel = asint(FaceTexelOrigins[Face]) + PointWhole;
	Point.PlanarCm =
		(float2(Point.GlobalTexel - ReferenceCameraTexel) + Point.PointFrac
			- ReferenceCameraTexelFrac) * TexelToLocalCm;
	return Point;
}

FArcTerrainTessSample ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(uint Face, float2 FacePoint)
{
	const FArcTerrainTessPlanarPoint Point =
		ArcTerrainTess_ResolvePlanarPoint(Face, FacePoint, CameraTexel, CameraTexelFrac);
	const FArcTerrainTessTierHit Hit = ArcTerrainTess_ResolveHeightTier(Point.GlobalTexel);
	const int Shift = ArcTerrainTess_HeightTierShift(Hit.Tier);
	const int2 CoarseTexel = Point.GlobalTexel >> Shift;
	const int2 SectorKey = CoarseTexel >> SectorQuadsShift;

	FArcTerrainTessSample Sample;
	// The window is the bounding square of the resident set, so a key inside it can still be a hole and
	// hold the fill slice. The fill slice is reserved past the allocatable range, so no sector names it.
	Sample.bResident = Hit.Slice != HeightFillSlice;
	Sample.GlobalTexel = Point.GlobalTexel;
	Sample.SectorKey = SectorKey;
	Sample.Slice = Hit.Slice;
	Sample.Tier = Hit.Tier;
	const int2 SectorLocalTexel = CoarseTexel - (SectorKey << SectorQuadsShift) + 1;
	const float2 TexelFrac =
		(Point.PointFrac + float2(Point.GlobalTexel - (CoarseTexel << Shift))) / float(1 << Shift);
	const float2 TileUV = (float2(SectorLocalTexel) + TexelFrac + 0.5f) * InvTileResolution;
	Sample.HeightCm = HeightAtlas.SampleLevel(HeightSamplerBilinear, float3(TileUV, (float)Hit.Slice), 0);
	Sample.PlanarCm = Point.PlanarCm;
	return Sample;
}

/**
 * DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY legacy height error a split would REMOVE, not the error that is there: the whole edge's sag against its
 * chord, minus whatever the deeper of the two halves would still carry afterwards.
 *
 * On smooth ground a half sags a quarter as much, so this returns about three quarters of the sag and the
 * split is worth its triangles. Across a step in the heightmap — a cut at 90 degrees, or any cliff — the
 * half carries the SAME step, so this returns zero: the split moves the error, it does not reduce it, and
 * the ground stays at whatever depth it reached. That holds at every depth, not only at the ceiling.
 *
 * Every term is symmetric in the two ends: swapping C0 with C2 swaps the two halves, and max() does not
 * care. The winding matrix therefore cannot separate the two parents of a diamond, which share this edge.
 */
float ArcTerrainTess_ReducibleDeviationCm(uint Face, float2 C0, float2 C2, FArcTerrainTessSample S0,
	FArcTerrainTessSample S2, out FArcTerrainTessSample OutMid, out float3 OutDeviationCm,
	out bool bOutMeasured)
{
	const FArcTerrainTessSample Mid = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.5f * (C0 + C2));
	OutMid = Mid;
	OutDeviationCm = 0.0f;
	bOutMeasured = false;
	// The fill slice carries no surface, so a difference involving it measures the fill level, not terrain.
	// ALL THREE have to be resident: one resident end against a fill-slice end reports the elevation itself
	// as deviation, and that state occupies the whole residency perimeter every frame.
	if (!Mid.bResident || !S0.bResident || !S2.bResident)
	{
		return 0.0f;
	}
	bOutMeasured = true;

	const float WholeCm = abs(Mid.HeightCm - 0.5f * (S0.HeightCm + S2.HeightCm));

	const FArcTerrainTessSample QuarterLow = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.75f * C0 + 0.25f * C2);
	const FArcTerrainTessSample QuarterHigh = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.25f * C0 + 0.75f * C2);
	if (!QuarterLow.bResident || !QuarterHigh.bResident)
	{
		bOutMeasured = false;
		return 0.0f;
	}
	const float LowCm = abs(QuarterLow.HeightCm - 0.5f * (S0.HeightCm + Mid.HeightCm));
	const float HighCm = abs(QuarterHigh.HeightCm - 0.5f * (Mid.HeightCm + S2.HeightCm));

	OutDeviationCm = float3(WholeCm, LowCm, HighCm);
	return max(WholeCm - max(LowCm, HighCm), 0.0f);
}

float2 ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(float4 Clip)
{
	return (Clip.xy / Clip.w * 0.5f + 0.5f) * ViewportSize;
}

float ArcTerrainTess_MaxEdgePixels(float4 H0, float4 H1, float4 H2,
	float3 P0, float3 P1, float3 P2, float DistanceCm)
{
	if (min(min(H0.w, H1.w), H2.w) <= ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W
		|| !all(isfinite(H0)) || !all(isfinite(H1)) || !all(isfinite(H2)))
	{
		const float EdgeCm = max(max(length(P1 - P0), length(P2 - P1)), length(P0 - P2));
		return min(EdgeCm * PixelsPerRadian / max(DistanceCm, 1.0f), 3.402823e+38f);
	}

	const float2 V0 = ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(H0);
	const float2 V1 = ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(H1);
	const float2 V2 = ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(H2);
	const float MaxEdge = max(max(length(V1 - V0), length(V2 - V1)), length(V0 - V2));
	return isfinite(MaxEdge) ? MaxEdge : 3.402823e+38f;
}

float ArcTerrainTess_ProjectedHeightErrorPixels(FArcTerrainTessSample Sample, float PlaneHeightCm,
	out float OutDeviationCm)
{
	OutDeviationCm = abs(Sample.HeightCm - PlaneHeightCm);
	const float4 ActualClip = mul(
		float4(Sample.PlanarCm, Sample.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 PlaneClip = mul(
		float4(Sample.PlanarCm, PlaneHeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	if (!all(isfinite(ActualClip)) || !all(isfinite(PlaneClip)) || !isfinite(OutDeviationCm))
	{
		OutDeviationCm = 0.0f;
		return 0.0f;
	}
	// A perspective pixel error has no meaning on or behind the eye plane. Visibility and the finite
	// area/edge fallback own that case; turning it into FLT_MAX made every camera turn refine to the cap.
	if (min(ActualClip.w, PlaneClip.w) <= ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W)
	{
		return 0.0f;
	}

	const float ErrorPixels = length(
		ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(ActualClip) - ArcTerrainTess_ViewportPoint(PlaneClip));
	return isfinite(ErrorPixels) ? ErrorPixels : 3.402823e+38f;
}

/** Maximum displacement between four resident height probes and the CURRENT triangle plane. A future
 *  child retaining the displacement does not subtract it from the parent, which closes the old refinement
 *  deadlock. Unknown residency deliberately returns zero; callers retain the fill-slice relief/cap policy. */
float ArcTerrainTess_SampledGeometryError(FArcTerrainTessSample S0, FArcTerrainTessSample S1,
	FArcTerrainTessSample S2, FArcTerrainTessSample M01, FArcTerrainTessSample M12,
	FArcTerrainTessSample M20, FArcTerrainTessSample Centroid, out float OutErrorCm,
	out bool bOutMeasured)
{
	bOutMeasured = S0.bResident && S1.bResident && S2.bResident && M01.bResident && M12.bResident
		&& M20.bResident && Centroid.bResident;
	OutErrorCm = 0.0f;
	if (!bOutMeasured)
	{
		return 0.0f;
	}

	float D01;
	float D12;
	float D20;
	float DG;
	const float E01 = ArcTerrainTess_ProjectedHeightErrorPixels(M01,
		0.5f * (S0.HeightCm + S1.HeightCm), D01);
	const float E12 = ArcTerrainTess_ProjectedHeightErrorPixels(M12,
		0.5f * (S1.HeightCm + S2.HeightCm), D12);
	const float E20 = ArcTerrainTess_ProjectedHeightErrorPixels(M20,
		0.5f * (S2.HeightCm + S0.HeightCm), D20);
	const float EG = ArcTerrainTess_ProjectedHeightErrorPixels(Centroid,
		(S0.HeightCm + S1.HeightCm + S2.HeightCm) / 3.0f, DG);
	OutErrorCm = max(max(D01, D12), max(D20, DG));
	return max(max(E01, E12), max(E20, EG));
}

int ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingSubtractRadius(int Value, int Radius)
{
	const int MinInt = (-2147483647 - 1);
	return Value < MinInt + Radius ? MinInt : Value - Radius;
}

int ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingAddRadius(int Value, int Radius)
{
	const int MaxInt = 2147483647;
	return Value > MaxInt - Radius ? MaxInt : Value + Radius;
}

int2 ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(FArcTerrainTessSample Sample, uint Tier)
{
	return Sample.GlobalTexel >> (SectorQuadsShift + ArcTerrainTess_HeightTierShift(Tier));
}

bool ArcTerrainTess_FootprintOverlapsRing(uint Tier, int2 MinKey, int2 MaxKey)
{
	const int Radius = HeightRingRadius[Tier];
	if (Radius < 0)
	{
		return false;
	}

	const int2 Center = int2(HeightRingCenterX[Tier], HeightRingCenterY[Tier]);
	const int2 RingMin = int2(
		ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingSubtractRadius(Center.x, Radius),
		ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingSubtractRadius(Center.y, Radius));
	const int2 RingMax = int2(
		ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingAddRadius(Center.x, Radius),
		ArcTerrainTess_SaturatingAddRadius(Center.y, Radius));
	return all(MinKey <= RingMax) && all(MaxKey >= RingMin);
}

struct FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution
{
	float2 HeightRangeCm;
	int2   SectorKey;
	uint   Tier;
	uint   Slice;
	uint   Source;
};

FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution ArcTerrainTess_GlobalHeightRangeResolution(uint Source)
{
	FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution Result;
	Result.HeightRangeCm = ConservativeHeightRangeCm;
	Result.SectorKey = 0;
	Result.Tier = NumHeightTiers;
	Result.Slice = HeightFillSlice;
	Result.Source = Source;
	return Result;
}

/**
 * Resolves a range only when the complete closed footprint is covered by one known height source.
 * Each point's integer texel is its exact half-open-domain owner, including points on sector borders.
 * A multi-sector bbox touching a finer residency ring could contain an overlay missed by the corners;
 * refusing it is conservative and avoids a variable-size ring scan per triangle.
 */
FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution ArcTerrainTess_ResolveFootprintHeightRange(
	FArcTerrainTessSample S0, FArcTerrainTessSample S1, FArcTerrainTessSample S2)
{
	FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution Result =
		ArcTerrainTess_GlobalHeightRangeResolution(ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_UNSAFE);

	UNROLL
	for (uint T = 0u; T < 4u; ++T)
	{
		if (T >= NumHeightTiers)
		{
			break;
		}

		const int2 K0 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S0, T);
		const int2 K1 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S1, T);
		const int2 K2 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S2, T);
		const int2 MinKey = min(min(K0, K1), K2);
		const int2 MaxKey = max(max(K0, K1), K2);
		const bool bSingleSector = all(MinKey == MaxKey);
		const bool bOverlapsRing = ArcTerrainTess_FootprintOverlapsRing(T, MinKey, MaxKey);

		if (!bSingleSector)
		{
			if (bOverlapsRing)
			{
				Result.Source = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_SPAN;
				Result.Tier = T;
				Result.SectorKey = MinKey;
				return Result;
			}
			continue;
		}

		if (!bOverlapsRing)
		{
			continue;
		}

		// The sampling walk has already read this one ring cell at every corner. Once all finer
		// tiers have been excluded, a hit at this tier must therefore agree at all three points.
		const bool bHit0 = S0.Tier == T && all(S0.SectorKey == MinKey);
		const bool bHit1 = S1.Tier == T && all(S1.SectorKey == MinKey);
		const bool bHit2 = S2.Tier == T && all(S2.SectorKey == MinKey);
		if (bHit0 || bHit1 || bHit2)
		{
			Result.Tier = T;
			Result.SectorKey = MinKey;
			Result.Slice = bHit0 ? S0.Slice : (bHit1 ? S1.Slice : S2.Slice);
			if (!(bHit0 && bHit1 && bHit2) || S0.Slice != S1.Slice || S0.Slice != S2.Slice)
			{
				Result.Source = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_SPAN;
				return Result;
			}
			if (S0.Slice >= HeightSliceBoundsCount)
			{
				return Result;
			}

			const float2 SliceRange = HeightSliceBounds[S0.Slice];
			if (!all(isfinite(SliceRange)) || SliceRange.x > SliceRange.y)
			{
				return Result;
			}
			Result.HeightRangeCm = SliceRange;
			Result.Source = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_LOCAL;
			return Result;
		}

		// Reaching a coarser tier after a finer sample hit would mean the footprint proof and the
		// sample resolver disagree. Keep that impossible state conservative rather than indexing metadata.
		if (S0.Tier < T || S1.Tier < T || S2.Tier < T)
		{
			Result.Tier = T;
			Result.SectorKey = MinKey;
			return Result;
		}
	}

	if (S0.bResident || S1.bResident || S2.bResident)
	{
		return Result;
	}

	// Fill is globally flat, but accept it only once the footprint is one sector at the coarsest
	// published domain (or the base domain when no tier exists) and every possible overlay was excluded.
	const uint FillTier = NumHeightTiers > 0u ? NumHeightTiers - 1u : 0u;
	const int2 FillK0 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S0, FillTier);
	const int2 FillK1 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S1, FillTier);
	const int2 FillK2 = ArcTerrainTess_SectorKeyForTier(S2, FillTier);
	if (!all(FillK0 == FillK1) || !all(FillK0 == FillK2))
	{
		Result.Source = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_SPAN;
		Result.Tier = FillTier;
		Result.SectorKey = min(min(FillK0, FillK1), FillK2);
		return Result;
	}

	Result.Tier = FillTier;
	Result.SectorKey = FillK0;
	if (isfinite(BaseHeightCm))
	{
		Result.HeightRangeCm = BaseHeightCm.xx;
		Result.Source = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_FILL;
	}
	return Result;
}

/**
 * Whether the conservative resolved-height prism over the planar triangle lies wholly outside the view.
 *
 * Gribb-Hartmann in its clip-space form: the four side planes of EyeLocalToClip are w +- x and w +- y, so
 * a corner's signed distance to each is a linear function of its clip position and the test needs no
 * perspective divide — it stays exact for a corner behind the eye, where the divide flips sign. The margin
 * widens each side plane into the half-space x + w(1 + m) >= 0, which CONTAINS the true frustum for every
 * m >= 0 at either sign of w: on the frustum w is positive, so the extra m*w only ever adds. A corner
 * behind the eye is therefore judged against a half-space that still covers everything visible, and the
 * complement being a half-space too is what makes the vertex test valid on the whole prism.
 *
 * The prism is rejected only when ALL SIX corners fall outside ONE plane. That is what keeps a
 * shallow base-mesh leaf thousands of kilometres wide that CONTAINS the whole frustum: it crosses every
 * plane rather than sitting outside any of them, so no test fires and it stays visible.
 */
bool ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCullHeightPrism(FArcTerrainTessSample S0, FArcTerrainTessSample S1,
	FArcTerrainTessSample S2, float Margin,
	out FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution OutResolution)
{
	OutResolution = ArcTerrainTess_GlobalHeightRangeResolution(ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_GLOBAL_UNSAFE);
	BRANCH
	if (LocalHeightBoundsEnabled != 0u)
	{
		OutResolution = ArcTerrainTess_ResolveFootprintHeightRange(S0, S1, S2);
	}

	const float MinHeightCm = OutResolution.HeightRangeCm.x - ViewHeightLocalCm;
	const float MaxHeightCm = OutResolution.HeightRangeCm.y - ViewHeightLocalCm;
	const float4 H0Min = mul(float4(S0.PlanarCm, MinHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H1Min = mul(float4(S1.PlanarCm, MinHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H2Min = mul(float4(S2.PlanarCm, MinHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H0Max = mul(float4(S0.PlanarCm, MaxHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H1Max = mul(float4(S1.PlanarCm, MaxHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H2Max = mul(float4(S2.PlanarCm, MaxHeightCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);

	// Non-finite clip coordinates cannot prove the prism invisible.
	if (!all(isfinite(H0Min)) || !all(isfinite(H1Min)) || !all(isfinite(H2Min))
		|| !all(isfinite(H0Max)) || !all(isfinite(H1Max)) || !all(isfinite(H2Max)))
	{
		return false;
	}

	// The prism is the convex hull of its six corners and w is affine in position, so all six corners at
	// or behind the eye plane put the whole prism there.
	if (max(max(max(H0Min.w, H1Min.w), max(H2Min.w, H0Max.w)), max(H1Max.w, H2Max.w))
		<= ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W)
	{
		return true;
	}

	const float3 XMin = float3(H0Min.x, H1Min.x, H2Min.x);
	const float3 YMin = float3(H0Min.y, H1Min.y, H2Min.y);
	const float3 WMin = float3(H0Min.w, H1Min.w, H2Min.w) * (1.0f + max(Margin, 0.0f));
	const float3 XMax = float3(H0Max.x, H1Max.x, H2Max.x);
	const float3 YMax = float3(H0Max.y, H1Max.y, H2Max.y);
	const float3 WMax = float3(H0Max.w, H1Max.w, H2Max.w) * (1.0f + max(Margin, 0.0f));
	return (all(XMin < -WMin) && all(XMax < -WMax))
		|| (all(XMin > WMin) && all(XMax > WMax))
		|| (all(YMin < -WMin) && all(YMax < -WMax))
		|| (all(YMin > WMin) && all(YMax > WMax));
}

bool ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCulled(float4 H0, float4 H1, float4 H2, float Margin)
{
	if (!all(isfinite(H0)) || !all(isfinite(H1)) || !all(isfinite(H2)))
	{
		return false;
	}
	if (max(max(H0.w, H1.w), H2.w) <= ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W)
	{
		return true;
	}

	const float3 X = float3(H0.x, H1.x, H2.x);
	const float3 Y = float3(H0.y, H1.y, H2.y);
	const float3 W = float3(H0.w, H1.w, H2.w) * (1.0f + max(Margin, 0.0f));
	return all(X < -W) || all(X > W) || all(Y < -W) || all(Y > W);
}

/** Finite planar discovery size for a sampled triangle whose authored-height prism still intersects the
 *  tessellation frustum. Edge / PI is the near-distance floor: when the camera enters the footprint's
 *  enclosing circle the score is therefore bounded by PI * PixelsPerRadian rather than exploding at zero. */
float ArcTerrainTess_PrismDiscoveryEdgePixels(float2 P0, float2 P1, float2 P2)
{
	const float DiscoveryPi = 3.14159265358979323846f;
	const float EdgeCm = max(max(length(P1 - P0), length(P2 - P1)), length(P0 - P2));
	const float2 Center = (P0 + P1 + P2) / 3.0f;
	const float Radius = max(max(length(P0 - Center), length(P1 - Center)), length(P2 - Center));
	const float MinDistanceCm = max(EdgeCm / DiscoveryPi, 1.0f);
	const float NearDistanceCm = max(length(Center) - Radius, MinDistanceCm);
	return min(EdgeCm * PixelsPerRadian / NearDistanceCm, DiscoveryPi * PixelsPerRadian);
}

/**
 * The second entry point of this file, and the only one that is not a tessellation verdict: whether the
 * triangle can be left out of a draw. It takes the same corners in the same domain and reads the same view
 * block. The sampled surface rejects the common case; the authored-height prism is consulted only when
 * those corners are outside, retaining a possible ridge without making the global height range normal visibility.
 */
bool ArcTerrain_FrustumCullTriangle(uint Face, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2)
{
	const FArcTerrainTessSample S0 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C0);
	const FArcTerrainTessSample S1 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C1);
	const FArcTerrainTessSample S2 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C2);
	const float4 H0 = mul(float4(S0.PlanarCm, S0.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H1 = mul(float4(S1.PlanarCm, S1.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H2 = mul(float4(S2.PlanarCm, S2.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	if (!ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCulled(H0, H1, H2, FrustumCullMargin))
	{
		return false;
	}
	FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution ResolutionIgnored;
	return ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCullHeightPrism(
		S0, S1, S2, FrustumCullMargin, ResolutionIgnored);
}

/**
 * Screen area in square pixels of the three eye-relative corners.
 *
 * A vertex at or below ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W sits on or behind the eye plane, where the perspective divide
 * has no meaning and its sign flip would drive random subdivision. The whole triangle then falls back to
 * PixelsPerRadian^2 * Area3D / Distance^2 — the projected area of the same triangle turned to face the
 * eye, so it DROPS the grazing cosine and is an upper bound on what the projected form will ask for. A
 * leaf therefore crosses into view already fine enough and never climbs a level on a camera turn, which
 * is the property this branch exists for; it still tracks distance, so it cannot freeze either.
 */
float ArcTerrainTess_ScreenAreaPixels(float4 H0, float4 H1, float4 H2, float3 P0, float3 P1, float3 P2,
	float DistanceCm, out bool bOutFallback)
{
	bOutFallback = min(min(H0.w, H1.w), H2.w) <= ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W;

	if (bOutFallback)
	{
		const float Area3DCm2 = 0.5f * length(cross(P1 - P0, P2 - P0));
		return Area3DCm2 * PixelsPerRadian * PixelsPerRadian / (DistanceCm * DistanceCm);
	}

	const float2 S0 = H0.xy / H0.w * 0.5f + 0.5f;
	const float2 S1 = H1.xy / H1.w * 0.5f + 0.5f;
	const float2 S2 = H2.xy / H2.w * 0.5f + 0.5f;
	const float AreaNDC =
		0.5f * abs(S0.x * (S1.y - S2.y) + S2.x * (S0.y - S1.y) + S1.x * (S2.y - S0.y));
	return AreaNDC * ViewportSize.x * ViewportSize.y;
}

/** Every input the verdict was reached from, for the ProbePredicate dump. Diagnostic only: nothing here
 *  is read by the metric. The legacy comparison adds its two quarter samples only in the diagnostic
 *  permutation; a caller that ignores the whole struct pays for none of them. */
struct FArcTerrainTessProbe
{
	float2 C0;
	float2 C1;
	float2 C2;
	float3 P0;
	float3 P1;
	float3 P2;
	float3 ClipW;
	float3 DeviationCm;
	float4 HeightsCm;      // S0 S1 S2 M20, terrain-local
	float  EdgePixels;
	float  EffectiveMaxEdgePixels;
	float  LegacyReducibleErrorCm;
	float  MinClipW;
	/** The quotient the flat-area relief reads, not the sag itself. */
	float  SagCmPerMeterSq;
	uint   LeafTier;
	uint   LeafCapDepth;
	bool   bCornerTiersDiffer;
	bool   bErrorMeasured;
	bool   bResident0;
	bool   bResident1;
	bool   bResident2;
	bool   bResidentMid;
	bool   bFallback;
	bool   bFillOnly;
	bool   bAtCeiling;
	uint   VisibilityState;
	float  DiscoveryEdgePixels;
	float  DiscoveryTargetPixels;
	uint   HeightRangeSource;
	uint   HeightRangeTier;
	int2   HeightRangeSectorKey;
	uint   HeightRangeSlice;
	float2 HeightRangeCm;
};

/** The verdict plus everything it was reached from. OutErrorCm is the deviation in cm, before the
 *  projection. The tessellation cull first judges sampled {C0, CullApex, C2}; its authored-height prism
 *  only guards a possible hidden feature. bCullOnApex replaces C1 only for that footprint. */
int ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleProbe(uint Face, uint Depth, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2,
	bool bCullOnApex, float2 CullApex, bool bSkipTessFrustumCull,
	out float OutAreaPixels, out float OutErrorPixels, out float OutErrorCm, out float OutDistanceCm,
	out float OutEffectiveTargetPixels, out FArcTerrainTessProbe OutProbe);

/** The verdict plus the quantities it was reached from, for a caller that has to explain WHY a triangle
 *  reads the way it does. OutEffectiveTargetPixels is the area threshold this triangle was actually held
 *  to. */
int ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleDiag(uint Face, uint Depth, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2,
	out float OutAreaPixels, out float OutErrorPixels, out float OutErrorCm, out float OutDistanceCm,
	out float OutEffectiveTargetPixels)
{
	FArcTerrainTessProbe ProbeIgnored;
	return ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleProbe(Face, Depth, C0, C1, C2, false, C1, false, OutAreaPixels,
		OutErrorPixels, OutErrorCm, OutDistanceCm, OutEffectiveTargetPixels, ProbeIgnored);
}

/** Diagnostic verdict for a triangle the draw compaction has already proved visible. It intentionally
 *  bypasses TessFrustumCullMargin: that wider predictive frustum is the policy under measurement, not
 *  a reason to hide visible post-update debt from the latency audit. */
int ArcTerrain_ClassifyVisibleTriangleDiag(uint Face, uint Depth, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2,
	out float OutAreaPixels, out float OutErrorPixels, out float OutErrorCm, out float OutDistanceCm,
	out float OutEffectiveTargetPixels, out FArcTerrainTessProbe OutProbe)
{
	return ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleProbe(Face, Depth, C0, C1, C2, false, C1, true, OutAreaPixels,
		OutErrorPixels, OutErrorCm, OutDistanceCm, OutEffectiveTargetPixels, OutProbe);
}

/**
 * The single entry point. Corners are in the face's [0,1]^2 domain, in the order the LEB decode
 * produced them: C0 and C2 span the edge a split bisects, C1 is the apex.
 */
int ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangle(uint Face, uint Depth, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2)
{
	float AreaPixelsIgnored;
	float ErrorPixelsIgnored;
	float ErrorCmIgnored;
	float DistanceCmIgnored;
	float EffectiveTargetIgnored;
	return ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleDiag(Face, Depth, C0, C1, C2, AreaPixelsIgnored,
		ErrorPixelsIgnored, ErrorCmIgnored, DistanceCmIgnored, EffectiveTargetIgnored);
}

int ArcTerrain_ClassifyTriangleProbe(uint Face, uint Depth, float2 C0, float2 C1, float2 C2,
	bool bCullOnApex, float2 CullApex, bool bSkipTessFrustumCull,
	out float OutAreaPixels, out float OutErrorPixels, out float OutErrorCm, out float OutDistanceCm,
	out float OutEffectiveTargetPixels, out FArcTerrainTessProbe OutProbe)
{
	OutProbe = (FArcTerrainTessProbe)0;
	OutAreaPixels = 0.0f;
	OutDistanceCm = 0.0f;
	OutErrorPixels = 0.0f;
	OutErrorCm = 0.0f;
	OutEffectiveTargetPixels = TargetTrianglePixels;
	OutProbe.C0 = C0;
	OutProbe.C1 = C1;
	OutProbe.C2 = C2;
	OutProbe.MinClipW = ARC_TESS_MIN_CLIP_W;
	OutProbe.VisibilityState = ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_ORDINARY;
	OutProbe.HeightRangeSource = ARC_TESS_HEIGHT_SOURCE_UNKNOWN;
	OutProbe.HeightRangeTier = NumHeightTiers;
	OutProbe.HeightRangeSlice = HeightFillSlice;
	OutProbe.HeightRangeCm = ConservativeHeightRangeCm;

	const FArcTerrainTessSample S0 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C0);
	const FArcTerrainTessSample S1 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C1);
	const FArcTerrainTessSample S2 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, C2);
	const float3 P0 = float3(S0.PlanarCm, S0.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm);
	const float3 P1 = float3(S1.PlanarCm, S1.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm);
	const float3 P2 = float3(S2.PlanarCm, S2.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm);

	// The camera is the origin of this space. One centimetre is the floor, so a triangle the eye sits on
	// reads as enormous instead of dividing by zero; the depth ceiling bounds the refinement that follows.
	const float DistanceCm = max(length(0.5f * (P0 + P2)), 1.0f);
	const float4 H0 = mul(float4(P0, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H1 = mul(float4(P1, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
	const float4 H2 = mul(float4(P2, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);

	OutDistanceCm = DistanceCm;

	OutProbe.P0 = P0;
	OutProbe.P1 = P1;
	OutProbe.P2 = P2;
	OutProbe.ClipW = float3(H0.w, H1.w, H2.w);
	OutProbe.HeightsCm = float4(S0.HeightCm, S1.HeightCm, S2.HeightCm, 0.0f);
	OutProbe.bResident0 = S0.bResident;
	OutProbe.bResident1 = S1.bResident;
	OutProbe.bResident2 = S2.bResident;

	const bool bFillOnly = !S0.bResident && !S1.bResident && !S2.bResident;
	OutProbe.bFillOnly = bFillOnly;
	const uint CornerTier = ArcTerrainTess_LeafTier(S0.Tier, S1.Tier, S2.Tier);
	OutProbe.LeafTier = CornerTier;
	OutProbe.LeafCapDepth = bFillOnly ? ArcTerrainTess_FillCapDepth() : (uint)max(ResidentCapDepth, 0);
	const uint MinCornerTier = min(min(ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(S0.Tier),
		ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(S1.Tier)), ArcTerrainTess_CapTier(S2.Tier));
	OutProbe.bCornerTiersDiffer = MinCornerTier != CornerTier;
	OutProbe.bAtCeiling = Depth >= OutProbe.LeafCapDepth;

	// Fill-only is a representability ceiling, not a visibility policy. It wins before discovery so a
	// conservative authored prism cannot hold unloaded flat terrain above its sector-sized cap.
	if (bFillOnly && OutProbe.bAtCeiling)
	{
		return ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE;
	}

	// The sampled surface is the normal visibility test. The much taller authored prism is only a guard:
	// its bounded discovery score alone can request refinement.
	bool bPrismGuarded = false;
	if (!bSkipTessFrustumCull)
	{
		float4 HCull = H1;
		float2 PCull = S1.PlanarCm;
		FArcTerrainTessSample CullSample = S1;
		if (bCullOnApex)
		{
			const FArcTerrainTessSample SCull = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, CullApex);
			CullSample = SCull;
			PCull = SCull.PlanarCm;
			HCull = mul(float4(PCull, SCull.HeightCm - ViewHeightLocalCm, 1.0f), EyeLocalToClip);
		}

		if (ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCulled(H0, HCull, H2, TessFrustumCullMargin))
		{
			FArcTerrainTessHeightRangeResolution HeightRangeResolution;
			const bool bPrismCulled = ArcTerrainTess_FrustumCullHeightPrism(
				S0, CullSample, S2, TessFrustumCullMargin, HeightRangeResolution);
			OutProbe.HeightRangeSource = HeightRangeResolution.Source;
			OutProbe.HeightRangeTier = HeightRangeResolution.Tier;
			OutProbe.HeightRangeSectorKey = HeightRangeResolution.SectorKey;
			OutProbe.HeightRangeSlice = HeightRangeResolution.Slice;
			OutProbe.HeightRangeCm = HeightRangeResolution.HeightRangeCm;
			if (bPrismCulled)
			{
				OutProbe.VisibilityState = ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_PRISM_CULLED;
				return ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE;
			}

			bPrismGuarded = true;
			OutProbe.VisibilityState = ARC_TESS_VISIBILITY_PRISM_GUARDED;
			const float DiscoveryEdgePixels = ArcTerrainTess_PrismDiscoveryEdgePixels(
				S0.PlanarCm, PCull, S2.PlanarCm);
			const float DiscoveryTargetPixels =
				MaxTriangleEdgePixels * sqrt(max(FlatAreaRelief, 1.0f));
			OutProbe.DiscoveryEdgePixels = DiscoveryEdgePixels;
			OutProbe.DiscoveryTargetPixels = DiscoveryTargetPixels;
			if (DiscoveryEdgePixels > DiscoveryTargetPixels)
			{
				return ARC_TESS_TOO_COARSE;
			}
			if (DiscoveryEdgePixels >= DiscoveryTargetPixels * MergeThresholdFraction)
			{
				return ARC_TESS_KEEP;
			}
		}
	}

	const FArcTerrainTessSample M01 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.5f * (C0 + C1));
	const FArcTerrainTessSample M12 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.5f * (C1 + C2));
	const FArcTerrainTessSample M20 = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, 0.5f * (C2 + C0));
	const FArcTerrainTessSample Centroid = ArcTerrainTess_SampleFacePoint(Face, (C0 + C1 + C2) / 3.0f);
	OutProbe.HeightsCm.w = M20.HeightCm;
	OutProbe.bResidentMid = M20.bResident;

	bool bFallback;
	const float AreaPixels =
		ArcTerrainTess_ScreenAreaPixels(H0, H1, H2, P0, P1, P2, DistanceCm, bFallback);
	const float EdgePixels = ArcTerrainTess_MaxEdgePixels(H0, H1, H2, P0, P1, P2, DistanceCm);
	OutAreaPixels = AreaPixels;
	OutProbe.bFallback = bFallback;
	OutProbe.EdgePixels = EdgePixels;

	bool bErrorMeasured;
	float ErrorCm;
	const float ErrorPixels = ArcTerrainTess_SampledGeometryError(
		S0, S1, S2, M01, M12, M20, Centroid, ErrorCm, bErrorMeasured);

	OutErrorPixels = ErrorPixels;
	OutErrorCm = ErrorCm;
	OutProbe.bErrorMeasured = bErrorMeasured;

#if ARC_CBT_PROBE_PREDICATE
	FArcTerrainTessSample LegacyMid;
	bool bLegacyMeasured;
	OutProbe.LegacyReducibleErrorCm = ArcTerrainTess_ReducibleDeviationCm(
		Face, C0, C2, S0, S2, LegacyMid, OutProbe.DeviationCm, bLegacyMeasured);
#endif

	// The verdict remains TOO_COARSE at the hard representability ceiling so diagnostics retain unresolved
	// height/edge debt. The topology gate is the sole owner of whether a split can actually be emitted.
	OutProbe.bAtCeiling = Depth >= OutProbe.LeafCapDepth;

	// Sag over a smooth surface grows with the SQUARE of the span it is measured across, so dividing it by
	// that square is what makes a parent and its children read the same flatness and take the same relief.
	const float EdgeCmSq = max(max(dot(S1.PlanarCm - S0.PlanarCm, S1.PlanarCm - S0.PlanarCm),
		dot(S2.PlanarCm - S1.PlanarCm, S2.PlanarCm - S1.PlanarCm)),
		max(dot(S0.PlanarCm - S2.PlanarCm, S0.PlanarCm - S2.PlanarCm), 1.0f));
	// Divide before converting m^2 to avoid overflowing when the conservative near-plane path returns
	// FLT_MAX. The clamp is still far above any threshold the authored property can express.
	const float SagCmPerMeterSq = min(ErrorCm / EdgeCmSq, 3.0e34f) * 10000.0f;

	OutProbe.SagCmPerMeterSq = SagCmPerMeterSq;
	const float FlatWeight =
		bErrorMeasured ? saturate(SagCmPerMeterSq / FlatReliefSagCmPerMeterSq) : 0.0f;
	const float EffectiveTargetPixels = TargetTrianglePixels * lerp(FlatAreaRelief, 1.0f, FlatWeight);
	// Area relief changes a triangle budget by area. Apply its square root to the edge budget so flat and
	// unknown terrain keeps the same linear density instead of the 24 px discovery bound defeating the
	// relief and driving the CBT to its cap. Detected curvature continuously restores the authored bound.
	const float EffectiveMaxEdgePixels = MaxTriangleEdgePixels
		* lerp(sqrt(max(FlatAreaRelief, 1.0f)), 1.0f, FlatWeight);
	OutEffectiveTargetPixels = EffectiveTargetPixels;
	OutProbe.EffectiveMaxEdgePixels = EffectiveMaxEdgePixels;

	// No quotient form: a ratio rounds, so a value half an ulp above its threshold compares equal to 1.0
	// and flips the verdict.
	int MetricVerdict = ARC_TESS_KEEP;
	if (AreaPixels > EffectiveTargetPixels || ErrorPixels > TargetErrorPixels
		|| EdgePixels > EffectiveMaxEdgePixels)
	{
		MetricVerdict = ARC_TESS_TOO_COARSE;
	}
	else if (AreaPixels < EffectiveTargetPixels * MergeThresholdFraction
		&& ErrorPixels < TargetErrorPixels * MergeThresholdFraction
		&& EdgePixels < EffectiveMaxEdgePixels * MergeThresholdFraction)
	{
		MetricVerdict = ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE;
	}

	// The full metric cannot raise a split in the conservative prism halo. It only confirms that a
	// discovery-fine footprint is also genuinely fine enough to merge.
	return bPrismGuarded
		? (MetricVerdict == ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE ? ARC_TESS_TOO_FINE : ARC_TESS_KEEP)
		: MetricVerdict;
}
